    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42788bb6_64f9481d",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T16:24:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What context/task you do expect these function to get called from? Only the PD task or maybe the the TCPC alert handler task. That would help me understand what the synchronization boundaries are",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bfedad8_763cbd85",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T22:18:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The plan:\nActive AP: AP sends host command. Host command calls pd_setup_vdm_request (based on host command args). Host command sets DPM request (essentially a flag), and the PD task reacts to it.\n\nPassive AP: PD task calls dpm_attempt_mode_entry. dpm_attempt_mode_entry sets up and schedules send_svdm_deferred. send_svdm_deferred spoofs the host command in an approximation of what the AP would do before sending the host command. The rest proceeds as above.\n\nIn this patchset, pd_setup_vdm_request is called from dpm_attempt_mode_entry (PD task) instead of the host command (hook or host command task). I expect that that call will move into the host command, but see the below comment.\n\nI don\u0027t think there would ever be a reason to call these from the TCPC alert handler. None of this stuff should happen until the PE is waiting in a ready state.",
      "parentUuid": "42788bb6_64f9481d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab58abc3_e338ed34",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 89,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note this currently assumes we\u0027ll only want to enter one mode per port (which is generally what we\u0027ll want, unless we start getting calls for Google VID support).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 89,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 89,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c75b2bec_aecbdf3c",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 89,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-28T21:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack. My intention is that this be an essentially non-functional change. In our OOB discussion of this general structure, I speculated that one mechanism for configuring different policies for different boards could be conditionally compiling different DPM files/functions/data structures.",
      "parentUuid": "ab58abc3_e338ed34",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 89,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 89,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "860aefc1_dc24cbbe",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T02:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per OOB discussion with Diana, honeybuns has complicated the idea of using a host command to do this. If we still want to use a host command for this purpose, it should be trivial to add vdm and vdo_cnt to ec_params_typec_ctrl, etc., and invoke pd_setup_vdm_request from within typec_control.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 119,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac746148_deb10ab2",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it\u0027s easier (and in line with what we plan for honeybuns, long-term) we can put off declaring or implementing the host command until later, and just have the DPM module set the DPM request directly.  That\u0027s by and large all the current HC is doing.",
      "parentUuid": "860aefc1_dc24cbbe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 119,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25c1bb68_a6c6284b",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
