    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d221fa09_9817d858",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1029,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T16:24:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "instead of coming up with our own locking access, what do you think about using a queue instead?\n\nAlso, we should have some notification or handling if we couldn\u0027t get exclusive access or there wasn\u0027t any room left in the queue.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1005,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1029,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6eea457_16ec3c9e",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1029,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A queue could be interesting, particularly if it includes a type with the message data.  Then for multi-type entries (like TBT with an active cable) they could all just dump into the queue and we can send out the queue as we\u0027re able.",
      "parentUuid": "d221fa09_9817d858",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1005,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1029,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13b16fbe_e8c0aad2",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1029,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T22:18:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll need to take a look at queues. I\u0027m not familiar with their semantics in the EC. If they provide a check-and-set-style atomic op, they might work well.\n\nI don\u0027t think there would be a great advantage to allowing the host (or anybody) to queue up multiple SVDMs in a row. In general, the next step in the sequences we want to support is dictated by the result of the last step. We might need something like this to accommodate TBT mode entry. I\u0027m not sure how tight the timing would be in a typical host-command round trip scenario.",
      "parentUuid": "d221fa09_9817d858",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1005,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1029,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b85050c9_3bdb248c",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1029,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-28T21:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Removing synchronization from this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "13b16fbe_e8c0aad2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1005,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1029,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1af6e70f_f3bc7549",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1055,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T02:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After further testing, I am fairly convinced that, at least in the sysjump case, this never happens. At ToT, with TCPMv2, I can see this function being called, but no Exit Mode ever sends.\n\nHow would people feel about deleting this for now and creating a bug to reimplement it in terms of the forthcoming host command/DPM interface? That makes synchronization a lot easier to think about and seems like the direction that we should go in the long run. At present, I assert that deleting this function body doesn\u0027t make things any worse.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1046,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1055,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68d3a5c9_903563c7",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1055,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not surprised the sysjump isn\u0027t working.  It doesn\u0027t look like the TC code is actually trying to send the VDM before notifying.  But I suppose that\u0027s a bug for another time.\n\nDoes exiting on shutdown work currently?  That I\u0027d worry about regressing on ToT",
      "parentUuid": "1af6e70f_f3bc7549",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1046,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1055,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aac8a886_9a6dc90c",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1055,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-28T21:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not seeing an Exit Mode when I shutdown either. That\u0027s also true for ToT and at the commit before I added SVID discovery. I guess this needs to be fixed, but I\u0027m removing synchronization from this CL. This function won\u0027t be any more broken than it was before.",
      "parentUuid": "68d3a5c9_903563c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1046,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1055,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7953cdea_3d843231",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Honestly, I have a TODO on my sticky note to remove partner_type entirely.  It\u0027s a remnant of the first cable probing implementation and it\u0027s too non-specific to be useful for a lot of cases (just has CABLE instead of SOP\u0027 or SOP\u0027\u0027)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1410,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1410,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56c389f7_63bc0e71",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-28T21:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My ultimate intention with these TODOs is to use tx_type and get rid of partner_type. I had envisioned including partner_type in the glorious deletion of PE_DO_PORT_DISCOVERY, along with vdm_cmd.",
      "parentUuid": "7953cdea_3d843231",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1410,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1410,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f9e554a_4c73acfb",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1536,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T02:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this a good place to do this?\n\n\nIt seems like I\u0027m crossing an interface boundary unnecessarily. I\u0027ve basically moved state from the PE to other files without creating independent state machines for that state (yet?). In the long run, the DPM, in particular, may be able to pull itself up by its bootstraps. For now, it seems like the DP and DPM state should stay interlocked with the PE to avoid a lot of additional complexity and keep this CL from getting even more enormous.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1533,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1536,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f300b15d_fa9f2765",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1536,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be valid to initialize them any time we\u0027re init-ing the discovery data.  The DPM needs to know we\u0027ve reset a port partner connection and that\u0027s about the most graceful way we can do it.",
      "parentUuid": "2f9e554a_4c73acfb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1533,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1536,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8a4661e_c1ae1af7",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1536,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T01:32:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "f300b15d_fa9f2765",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1533,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1536,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
