    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1d49bbf_b4da9ed0",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T02:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like we need to check the SVID here to know whether we can do any DP stuff, but for now, I didn\u0027t want to disturb how this state works more than necessary.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5044,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 5044,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b90d4558_ba2ecbea",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the SVID ends up getting checked in the attention consumption, so it could also be added there if preferred.  Depends on how you\u0027d like the modules to play with the old supported SVID structures going forward.",
      "parentUuid": "c1d49bbf_b4da9ed0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5044,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 5044,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9d588eb_c61c6771",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T01:32:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like it is checked in dfp_consume_attention (indirectly, outside of mode-specific code). It would make sense to set the DP ACKed state inside the DP-specific consumption functions, like svdm_dp_attention. Unfortunately, those are being overridden by numerous boards and thus seem like bad places to put things that should always run.\n\nI envision that the DP module would eventually contain all the DP-specific functions currently in usb_pd_alt_mode.c. If there is board-specific mux behavior, that should be in a board function that gets called by the generic function. I don\u0027t think board code should need to parse VDOs or set DP flags (which I guess should also be in the DP module eventually).\n\nIn the meantime, without dramatically expanding the scope of this CL, this seems like no worse a place than any for this code.",
      "parentUuid": "b90d4558_ba2ecbea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5044,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 5044,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8fed954a_328b8875",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5059,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T02:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally, I think the PE would probably hand these off to the DPM, and the DPM would in turn hand off DP stuff to the DP module. This seemed to me like a reasonable intermediate form, but I\u0027m interested in other perspectives.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5039,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 5059,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67008326_2b280e03",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5059,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T21:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense to me.  If we can keep all the SVID-specifics in the DPM I think that would be cleanest, so the PE doesn\u0027t have to care about them. \n\nIs the vision for the DPM module that it\u0027ll be totally unnecessary when the AP is driving?  Or will it be handling the DPM interfacing like queuing up notifications to the AP, and have its autonomous behavior if\u0027d out?",
      "parentUuid": "8fed954a_328b8875",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5039,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 5059,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "173a0093_c2ee35d4",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5059,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-28T21:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If all the DPM is in charge of is mode management, then I would say that, in the long term, the AP should *be* the DPM, and the DPM module should be inert, with its basic DP functionality deactivated unless we\u0027re in recovery mode.\n\nIf we wanted to hew very close to the spec and make the PE basically unintelligent and hand those decisions off to the DPM, the DPM would still need to be doing stuff when the AP is driving, and it would probably make sense to have it also handle things like queuing and notifications.",
      "parentUuid": "67008326_2b280e03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5039,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 5059,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
